package.description:
Device Abstraction Layer Functions Package 1.0.
Bundles wishing to use this package must list the package in the Import-Package header of the bundle's manifest. This package has two types of users: the consumers that use the API in this package and the providers that implement the API in this package.
Example import for consumers using the API in this package:
{@code Import-Package: org.osgi.service.dal.functions; version="[1.0,2.0)"}
Example import for providers implementing the API in this package:
{@code Import-Package: org.osgi.service.dal.functions; version="[1.0,1.1)"}

class.description:
{@code BooleanControl} function provides a boolean control support. The
 eventable function state is accessible with {@link #getData()} getter and
 {@link #setData(boolean)} setter. The state can be reversed with
 {@link #inverse()} method, can be set to {@code true} value with
 {@link #setTrue()} method and can be set to {@code false} value with
 {@link #setFalse()} method.


 The control type can be:


{@link Types#LIGHT}

{@link Types#DOOR}

{@link Types#WINDOW}

{@link Types#POWER}

other type defined in {@link Types}

custom - vendor specific type

field.description:
Specifies the operation name, which sets the control state to
 {@code true} value. The operation can be executed with {@link #setTrue()}
 method.

class.description:
{@code BooleanSensor} function provides boolean sensor monitoring. It reports
 its state when an important event is available. The eventable state is
 accessible with {@link #getData()} getter. There are no operations.


 The sensor type can be:


{@link Types#LIGHT}

{@link Types#GAS}

{@link Types#SMOKE}

{@link Types#DOOR}

{@link Types#WINDOW}

{@link Types#POWER}

{@link Types#RAIN}

{@link Types#CONTACT}

{@link Types#FIRE}

{@link Types#OCCUPANCY}

{@link Types#WATER}

{@link Types#MOTION}

other type defined in {@link Types}

custom - vendor specific type

{@code Meter} function can measure metering information. The function
 provides these properties:


{@link #PROPERTY_CURRENT} - eventable property accessible with
 {@link #getCurrent()} getter;

{@link #PROPERTY_TOTAL} - eventable property accessible with
 {@link #getTotal()} getter.



 The sensor type can be:


{@link Types#PRESSURE}

{@link Types#GAS}

{@link Types#POWER}

{@link Types#WATER}

{@link Types#HEAT}

{@link Types#COLD}

other type defined in {@link Types}

custom - vendor specific type

field.description:
The service property value contains the metering flow. It's an optional
 property and available only if it's supported by the meter. The value
 type is {@code java.lang.String}. Possible property values:


{@link #FLOW_IN}

{@link #FLOW_OUT}

class.description:
{@code MultiLevelControl} function provides multi-level control support. The
 eventable function level is accessible with {@link #getData()} getter and
 {@link #setData(BigDecimal, String)} setter.


 The control type can be:


{@link Types#LIGHT}

{@link Types#TEMPERATURE}

{@link Types#FLOW}

{@link Types#PRESSURE}

{@link Types#HUMIDITY}

{@link Types#GAS}

{@link Types#SMOKE}

{@link Types#DOOR}

{@link Types#WINDOW}

{@link Types#LIQUID}

{@link Types#POWER}

{@link Types#NOISINESS}

other type defined in {@link Types}

custom - vendor specific type

{@code MultiLevelSensor} function provides multi-level sensor monitoring. It
 reports its state when an important event is available. The eventable state
 is accessible with {@link #getData()} getter. There are no operations.


 The sensor type can be:


{@link Types#LIGHT}

{@link Types#TEMPERATURE}

{@link Types#FLOW}

{@link Types#PRESSURE}

{@link Types#HUMIDITY}

{@link Types#GAS}

{@link Types#SMOKE}

{@link Types#DOOR}

{@link Types#WINDOW}

{@link Types#LIQUID}

{@link Types#POWER}

{@link Types#NOISINESS}

{@link Types#RAIN}

other type defined in {@link Types}

custom - vendor specific type

Shares common constants for all functions defined in this package. The
 defined function types are mapped as follow:


{@link #LIGHT} - {@link MultiLevelControl}, {@link MultiLevelSensor},
 {@link BooleanSensor} and {@link BooleanControl}

{@link #TEMPERATURE} - {@link MultiLevelControl} and
 {@link MultiLevelSensor}

{@link #FLOW} - {@link MultiLevelControl} and {@link MultiLevelSensor}

{@link #PRESSURE} - {@link MultiLevelControl}, {@link MultiLevelSensor}
 and {@link Meter}

{@link #HUMIDITY} - {@link MultiLevelControl} and
 {@link MultiLevelSensor}

{@link #GAS} - {@link MultiLevelControl}, {@link MultiLevelSensor},
 {@link BooleanSensor} and {@link Meter}

{@link #SMOKE} - {@link MultiLevelControl}, {@link MultiLevelSensor} and
 {@link BooleanSensor}

{@link #DOOR} - {@link MultiLevelControl}, {@link MultiLevelSensor},
 {@link BooleanSensor} and {@link BooleanControl}

{@link #WINDOW} - {@link MultiLevelControl}, {@link MultiLevelSensor},
 {@link BooleanSensor} and {@link BooleanControl}

{@link #LIQUID} - {@link MultiLevelControl} and {@link MultiLevelSensor}

{@link #POWER} - {@link MultiLevelControl}, {@link MultiLevelSensor},
 {@link BooleanSensor}, {@link BooleanControl} and {@link Meter}

{@link #NOISINESS} - {@link MultiLevelControl} and
 {@link MultiLevelSensor}

{@link #RAIN} - {@link MultiLevelSensor} and {@link BooleanSensor}

{@link #CONTACT} - {@link BooleanSensor}

{@link #FIRE} - {@link BooleanSensor}

{@link #OCCUPANCY} - {@link BooleanSensor}

{@link #WATER} - {@link BooleanSensor} and {@link Meter}

{@link #MOTION} - {@link BooleanSensor}

{@link #HEAT} - {@link Meter}

{@link #COLD} - {@link Meter}

 The mapping is not mandatory. The function can use custom defined types.

